// EXPECT: E0250 — a name promoted by two `using`s, reported at the *use* (ADR-0050 §3)
//
// This is ADR-0014 §3's ambiguity rule reused verbatim rather than a second one invented:
// overlapping providers are harmless as long as the ambiguous name is never referenced. So
// `qualified_only` below is **legal** — it uses only `a.x` and `b.y` — and only `ambiguous` is
// refused.
//
// Refusing at the *declaration* instead was considered and rejected: it would make two overlapping
// embeds illegal even in a procedure that only ever writes the qualified forms, which the import
// rules deliberately permit.
Point :: struct {
    x: s64;
    y: s64;
}

/// Legal: overlapping promotions, never used unqualified.
qualified_only :: (using a: Point, using b: Point) -> s64 {
    return a.x + b.y;
}

/// Refused: `x` could be either.
ambiguous :: (using a: Point, using b: Point) -> s64 {
    return x;
}
